\f0\fs24 \cf2 Viewing the grand salon from another perspective, we notice the wood paneling that once belonged to the choir of the Church of Classe di Dentro in Ravenna. This precious element enriches the room with a truly unique atmosphere. The wooden furnishings, carefully positioned, remain exactly where the Bagatti Valsecchi brothers originally placed them, preserving the room\'92s perfect harmony. The only missing element is the large 18th-century Anatolian carpet that once graced the space with its elegance. Every detail, from the panelling to the furniture, bears witness to the brothers\'92 meticulous planning and their desire to create a setting that reflected their refined taste and welcomed the most prestigious guests.\
